{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D"},"abstract":[{"text":"An implementation of A* for finding the shortest path between two vertices on a connected graph in 3D space.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AStar3D","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A* (A star) is a computer algorithm used in pathfinding and graph traversal, the process of plotting short paths among vertices (points), passing through a given set of edges (segments). It enjoys widespread use due to its performance and accuracy. Godot’s A* implementation uses points in 3D space and Euclidean distances by default."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You must add points manually with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/addPoint(id:position:weightScale:)","isActive":true},{"text":" and create segments manually with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/connectPoints(id:toId:bidirectional:)","isActive":true},{"text":". Once done, you can test if there is a path between two points with the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/arePointsConnected(id:toId:bidirectional:)","isActive":true},{"text":" function, get a path containing indices by ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/getIdPath(fromId:toId:allowPartialPath:)","isActive":true},{"text":", or one containing actual coordinates with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/getPointPath(fromId:toId:allowPartialPath:)","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It is also possible to use non-Euclidean distances. To do so, create a script that extends ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D","isActive":true},{"text":" and override the methods ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/_computeCost(fromId:toId:)","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/_estimateCost(fromId:endId:)","isActive":true},{"text":". Both should take two point IDs and return the distance between the corresponding points.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Example:"}]},{"text":" Use Manhattan distance instead of Euclidean distance:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/_estimateCost(fromId:endId:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" should return a lower bound of the distance, i.e. ","type":"text"},{"code":"_estimate_cost(u, v) <= _compute_cost(u, v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This serves as a hint to the algorithm because the custom ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/_computeCost(fromId:toId:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" might be computation-heavy. If this is not the case, make ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/_estimateCost(fromId:endId:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" return the same value as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/_computeCost(fromId:toId:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" to provide the algorithm with the most accurate information.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the default ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/_estimateCost(fromId:endId:)","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/_computeCost(fromId:toId:)","isActive":true},{"text":" methods are used, or if the supplied ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/_estimateCost(fromId:endId:)","isActive":true},{"text":" method returns a lower bound of the cost, then the paths returned by A* will be the lowest-cost paths. Here, the cost of a path equals the sum of the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/_computeCost(fromId:toId:)","isActive":true},{"text":" results of all segments in the path multiplied by the ","type":"text"},{"code":"weight_scale","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s of the endpoints of the respective segments. If the default methods are used and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"weight_scale","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s of all points are set to ","type":"text"},{"code":"1.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then this equals the sum of Euclidean distances of all segments in the path.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/_computeCost(fromId:toId:)","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/_estimateCost(fromId:endId:)","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AStar3D\/addPoint(id:position:weightScale:)","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodo